n\n$$\n{Y}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{Z}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba090db14c2dfc5f445393c04e1a961f648b91d0b9703749c30d55368772f329"} {"question" "q-22055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9257f8c40add6ab1b82355accdf9587b7750c84fd830461d2b204bd0b61c3bd"} {"question" "q-22055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba090db14c2dfc5f445393c04e1a961f648b91d0b9703749c30d55368772f329"} {"question" "q-22055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba090db14c2dfc5f445393c04e1a961f648b91d0b9703749c30d55368772f329"} {"question" "q-22055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba090db14c2dfc5f445393c04e1a961f648b91d0b9703749c30d55368772f329"} {"question" "q-129437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\n- The product $RS$ is well defined\n- The product $RP$ is well defined\n- The product $SP$ is well defined" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba090db14c2dfc5f445393c04e1a961f648b91d0b9703749c30d55368772f329"} {"question" "q-129437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $P$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{5\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $S$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba090db14c2dfc5f445393c04e1a961f648b91d0b9703749c30d55368772f329"} {"question" "q-129437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" 