le_sha256" "ba090db14c2dfc5f445393c04e1a961f648b91d0b9703749c30d55368772f329"} {"question" "q-129489" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\times 4"] ["math" "3\\times 4"] ["math" "4\\times 2"] ["math" "4\\times 4"] ["text" "The product is undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba090db14c2dfc5f445393c04e1a961f648b91d0b9703749c30d55368772f329"} {"question" "q-129489" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\times 4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba090db14c2dfc5f445393c04e1a961f648b91d0b9703749c30d55368772f329"} {"question" "e-4403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}19 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4403.json" "file_sha256" "25df0447da85d2d9cfe7903748737ca8c58ea38ab3dca22bb8c0d02d539e5aa4"} {"question" "e-4403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = \n\t{\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4403.json" "file_sha256" "25df0447da85d2d9cfe7903748737ca8c58ea38ab3dca22bb8c0d02d539e5aa4"} {"question" "e-4404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $A$ is a $3 \\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix. What are the dimensions of $AB$?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4404.json" "file_sha256" "ba40b60282c7702de045ff3bd76c567ea63daeb81dd2284c44223e8aeea09ccc"} {"question" "e-4404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "There are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication, and $AB$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{B} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{AB}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4404.json" "file_sha256" "ba40b60282c7702de045ff3bd76c567ea63daeb81dd2284c44223e8aeea09ccc"} {"question" "e-4405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4405.json" "file_sha256" "06a6a75f0633306bcd63df9227f33f6386016125bce8ffb3ab7207da4dd18d7b"} {"question" "e-4405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice that $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2 \\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2 \\times 2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{B} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{A} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{BA}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4405.json" "file_sha256" "06a6a75f0633306bcd63df9227f33f6386016125bce8ffb3ab7207da4dd18d7b"}] "usage" {"e-4405" [] "e-4404" [] "e-4403" []} "basis" 917 "retractions" [[17592186100604 :question/problem "Let\n$\\begin{bmatrix}19 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n2. The product $B\\times A$ is well defined"] [17592186100604 :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B$. Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B$, the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = {\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A$. Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A$, the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false."] [17592186100605 :question/worked-solution "There are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B$. Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B$, the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication, and $AB$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{B} = \\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{AB}\n$$"] [17592186100606 :question/problem "Let\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA$?"] [17592186100606 :question/worked-solution "We notice that $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2 \\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A$. Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A$, the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication.\n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2 \\times 2$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{B} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{A} = \\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{BA}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers"